{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.GenusFiltrationIdeal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.GenusFiltrationIdeal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Monic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.all_large_primes_obstructed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.all_large_primes_obstructed","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L294-L298","doc":"All primes p ≥ 11 are obstructed at the completeness-determined\ngenus g = 4.  Their Hecke coefficients lie in I_4 = (u^5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.leading_chebyshev_coeff_is_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.leading_chebyshev_coeff_is_one","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L270-L292","doc":"**The leading Chebyshev coefficient is 1** for all odd `p ≥ 3` —\ni.e. `a_p` is monic. This is what makes the Yekutieli obstruction\n`κ(T_{2,p})` nonzero whenever `(p-1)/2 > g`: the top coefficient\ncannot cancel.\n\nPreviously this was stated as the defining recurrence with\n`- s^(p-1)` added to both sides and closed by `ring` — a\nrearrangement of the definition, saying nothing about any leading\ncoefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genus4_cutoff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus4_cutoff","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L258-L264","doc":"At the completeness-determined genus g = 4:\nT_{2,p} embeds iff p ≤ 9. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.seifert_genus_le_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.seifert_genus_le_iff","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L250-L256","doc":"Arithmetic equivalence: (p-1)/2 ≤ g ↔ (p-1) ≤ 2g.\nLinks the Seifert genus bound to the embeddability condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_degree_eq_genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_degree_eq_genus","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L215-L244","doc":"**The Chebyshev degree equals the Seifert genus.**\n\nFor odd `p ≥ 3` the three conjuncts jointly say `deg_u a_p =\n(p-1)/2 = ` the Seifert genus of `T_{2,p}`:\n\n1. `a_p` has degree `p - 1` in `s`;\n2. only *even* powers of `s` occur, so `a_p` really is a polynomial\n   in `u = s²`, and its `u`-degree is half its `s`-degree;\n3. that half is exactly `seifertGenus_T2p p`.\n\nPreviously this was stated as `seifertGenus_T2p p = (p - 1) / 2`,\nwhich is `(p-1)/2 = (p-1)/2` by `rfl` — the binders `s` and\n`heckeCoeff` did not occur in the conclusion, so the claim carried\nnone of the content its docstring described. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckePoly_coeff_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckePoly_coeff_parity","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L174-L213","doc":"Every nonzero coefficient of `a_{n+1}` sits in a degree congruent to\n`n` mod 2. For odd `p` this says `a_p` is an *even* polynomial in `s`,\nwhich is what makes it a polynomial in `u = s²` at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckePoly_natDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckePoly_natDegree","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L171-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckePoly_monic_natDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckePoly_monic_natDegree","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L136-L168","doc":"`a_{n+1}` is monic of degree `n`.\n\nProved as a conjunction because the induction needs both halves at\nonce: the degree step needs the *leading coefficient* of the previous\nterm to be nonzero, and the monic step needs the previous *degree* to\ndominate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckePoly_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckePoly_two","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L131-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckePoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckePoly","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L116-L128","doc":"The same recurrence carried in `ℤ[X]` rather than in `R_q`.\n\n`heckeCoeff` above is stated for an arbitrary ring element `s : R_q`,\nwhich is the right shape for the skein narrative but the wrong shape\nfor a *degree* claim: `degree` is a property of a polynomial in a\nformal indeterminate, not of an element of the coefficient ring. So\nthe degree statements below are made about `heckePoly`, the same\nrecurrence with `s := X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.seifertGenus_T2p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.seifertGenus_T2p","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L112-L114","doc":"The Seifert genus of T_{2,p} is (p-1)/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckeCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckeCoeff","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L103-L110","doc":"The Hecke coefficient a_n: T^n = a_n · T + a_{n-1} · 1 in H_2(q).\nSatisfies the recurrence a_{n+1} = s · a_n + a_{n-1}\nwith a_0 = 0, a_1 = 1, where s = q - q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.minimal_complete_genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.minimal_complete_genus","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L89-L97","doc":"g = 4 is the minimal genus where completeness holds:\nat g = 3 we have < 5 knots, at g = 4 we have ≥ 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genus4_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus4_complete","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L77-L87","doc":"At genus 4, we have 6 embeddable torus knots —\nsufficient to span 5 irreps (rank 5 verified numerically). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genus3_insufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus3_insufficient","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L65-L75","doc":"At genus 3, we have at most 4 embeddable torus knots —\ninsufficient to span 5 irreps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusEmbeddable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusEmbeddable","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L60-L63","doc":"A torus knot T_{m,n} embeds in genus g iff (m-1)(n-1) ≤ 2g. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.total_irreps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.total_irreps","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L56-L58","doc":"Total irreps of H_2(q) ⊕ H_3(q) = 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckeIrreps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckeIrreps","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L49-L54","doc":"Number of irreps of H_n(q) = number of partitions of n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_param","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.R_q","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0}]}